<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

		<!-- NuGet package metadata -->
		<PackageId>NTokenizers</PackageId>
		<Version>8.0.0</Version>
		<Authors>crwsolutions</Authors>
		<Copyright>(c) crwsolutions</Copyright>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Description>Collection of stream-capable tokenizers for XML, JSON, HTML, YAML, TOML, Markdown, TypeScript, CSS, C#, SQL, Java, C, C++, Rust, Kotlin, Go, Swift and Python processing, plus a stream-capable Markdown to HTML converter (ToHtml API). See README for usage and details.</Description>
		<PackageDescription>Collection of stream-capable tokenizers for XML, JSON, HTML, YAML, TOML, Markdown, TypeScript, CSS, C#, SQL, Java, C, C++, Rust, Kotlin, Go, Swift and Python processing, plus a stream-capable Markdown to HTML converter (ToHtml API). See README for usage and details.</PackageDescription>
		<PackageTags>tokenizer;xml;json;yaml;toml;md;markdown;typescript;javascript;css;c#;csharp;sql;java;c;c++;cpp;rust;kotlin;go;swift;python;stream;streaming;parse;parsing;dotnet;tohtml;html</PackageTags>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/crwsolutions/ntokenizers</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://crwsolutions.github.io/ntokenizers</PackageProjectUrl>
		<Title>NTokenizers</Title>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>This is a major release with a breaking change to the streaming ToHtml API.

## Breaking change: WriteHtml* methods return the consumed Markdown text

The streaming ToHtml methods now return the consumed Markdown source text:

- `WriteHtmlAsync` (Stream and TextReader overloads) returns `Task&lt;string&gt;` instead of `Task`.
- `WriteHtmlDocumentAsync` (Stream and TextReader overloads) returns `Task&lt;string&gt;` instead of `Task`.

The returned string is the raw Markdown input exactly as consumed (the Stream overloads return the decoded text, with any BOM detected and stripped). The change is binary-breaking under NuGet semver; existing call sites that await the methods are source-compatible.

Use the returned string to keep the Markdown you just rendered — for example, to store a live AI assistant reply in a chat history.

The `ToHtmlAsync` and `ToHtmlDocumentAsync` methods are unchanged: they continue to return the HTML string.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
